KZ3 patch 1110 (SPU pass 84): the last check for the lock-line-reservation-lost event before a reservation is
replaced or dropped, and an opt-in lock-line stall snapshot (KZ3_LR_SNAP).

Only writers that go through spu_coh_notify_write* raise SPU_EVENT_LR as they land. A store that bypasses them is
seen only by the snapshot compare in rdch/rchcnt SPU_RdEventStat (spu_resv_lost_poll), and only while the
reservation is still valid. GETLLAR (same line: snapshot overwritten; other line: spu_resv_drop) and PUTLLC
(failure, or a drop for another line) ended the reservation without that compare, so the event hardware latches at
the store was never raised and an SPU that then waits for it sleeps. RPCS3 PR #5435 (read as a reference only)
orders its GETLLAR the same way: a last check for the event before the old reservation is replaced.

Now spu_resv_last_check (spu_coherency.c), on the SPU's own thread: valid reservation, line != snapshot -> CAS
resv_valid 1 -> 0 and raise SPU_EVENT_LR (a concurrent notifier wins or loses the same CAS: raised once). Called by
spu_resv_drop, by GETLLAR on the same line before the snapshot is overwritten, and by a failing PUTLLC on its own
line. KZ3_LR_LASTCHECK=0 = old behaviour.

spu_context gains an LR history (raises, last source NOTIFY/POLL/LASTCHECK, last line, LR acks, last committed
PUTLLC line, PUTLLC failures). KZ3_LR_SNAP=1 (off by default; KZ3_LR_SNAP_N snapshots per run, default 4) prints one
line per registered SPU context with that history, the reservation (valid, line, changed-under-snapshot), the event
mask/status and a class (never-written / unseen-write / not-advanced / missed-wake / no-lr-wait), plus the reserved
line's 32 words, at the first 2 s heartbeat of a parked channel wait and at a 4M GETLLAR spin on one line.

upstream test_spu_lockline_peer.c "a PUTLLC that fails its compare raises nothing": the peer is still untouched; the
one raise is now the failing SPU's own (its reservation was lost to the unannounced store).
Host test: tools/spu/test_lr_lastcheck.sh (passes; with KZ3_LR_LASTCHECK=0 its 4 missed-wake cases fail).

